<title>JAPAN: Japan MOF announces auto insurance deregulation.</title>
<headline>Japan MOF announces auto insurance deregulation.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance (MOF) officially announced on Tuesday that it had lifted a ban on mail-order sales of auto insurance policies as of today.</p>
<p>A ministry official told reporters that MOF was currently examining a number of applications for such sales from U.S. insurance companies in Japan.</p>
<p>However, the ministry will not change the current system of setting premium rates for auto insurance, he said.</p>
</text>
